11. ADVANCES, DEDUCTIONS, CREDITS, AND BALANCES

Provide a separate financial adjustment module.

Support:

- Advance payments.
- Advance deductions.
- Percentage deductions.
- Fixed deductions.
- Other authorized credits.
- Additional payments.
- Corrections and reversals.

Every adjustment must have a description, date, amount, adjustment type, associated team or payment, and creator.

Do not confuse an advance paid previously with an advance deduction applied to the current payable balance.

Use the following default formulas:

Labour subtotal = sum of all category amounts.

Overtime subtotal = sum of applicable overtime amounts.

Additional charges subtotal = sum of charge items.

Gross amount = labour subtotal + overtime subtotal + additional charges subtotal.

Final payable = gross amount + credits - deductions - advances applied.

An advance payment already deducted in an earlier transaction must not be deducted a second time.

Support an explicit alternative payment calculation only when configured and documented. Keep supplier or contractor bills separate from count-based labour attendance while allowing them to appear in the consolidated weekly summary.

