22. REQUIRED AUTOMATED TESTS

Write and run automated tests for the following.

Week boundaries

- Saturday starts a new reporting week.
- Friday is the last day of that week.
- A date on Sunday belongs to the correct Saturday–Friday period.
- Month-crossing weeks work correctly.
- Time zone handling does not shift dates unexpectedly.

Financial calculations

- 33 × ₹950 = ₹31,350.
- 59 × ₹1,400 = ₹82,600.
- 35 × ₹1,000 = ₹35,000.
- ₹82,600 + ₹35,000 = ₹1,17,600.
- ₹15,600 + ₹2,400 = ₹18,000.
- 6.25% × ₹17,100 = ₹1,068.75.
- ₹17,100 − ₹1,068.75 = ₹16,031.25.
- ₹2,84,800 − ₹2,10,000 = ₹74,800.
- Multiple additional charge lines sum correctly.
- Zero counts produce zero labour amounts.
- Decimal amounts and rounding work correctly.
- Manual overrides preserve both the calculated and final values.
- Applying an advance once changes payable correctly.
- The same advance cannot be deducted twice unintentionally.

Data integrity

- Updating a default rate does not change old weeks.
- Editing an entry updates the correct totals.
- Deleting or reversing an entry updates reports correctly.
- Multiple entries on the same day are supported.
- Merged summaries do not double-count transactions.
- Attendance merges preserve audit history.
- Concurrent or repeated submissions do not create accidental duplicates.
- Monthly totals reconcile according to the documented policy.

Authorization

- Unauthenticated users cannot read financial records.
- Staff cannot access admin-only operations.
- Staff cannot promote themselves to admin.
- Admin can access and correct all company records.
- Database RLS policies enforce the same restrictions as the UI.

Do not report tests as passing unless they have actually been executed.

